From: Azure Linux <azurelinux@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: require GStreamer MPEG-TS only when enabled

USE_GSTREAMER_MPEGTS defaults to OFF, and the MPEG-TS headers, calls, and
linkage are already guarded by that option. Do not require the helper
library just because video playback is enabled.

The MPEG-TS helper library has an unstable API and is not needed for core
rendering, video playback, WebAudio, or Media Source Extensions. Keep it
required when USE_GSTREAMER_MPEGTS is explicitly enabled.

diff --git a/Source/cmake/GStreamerChecks.cmake b/Source/cmake/GStreamerChecks.cmake
--- a/Source/cmake/GStreamerChecks.cmake
+++ b/Source/cmake/GStreamerChecks.cmake
@@ -9,9 +9,13 @@ if (USE_GSTREAMER)
       else ()
           set(GSTREAMER_COMPONENTS app pbutils)
           if (ENABLE_VIDEO)
-              list(APPEND GSTREAMER_COMPONENTS video mpegts tag gl)
+              list(APPEND GSTREAMER_COMPONENTS video tag gl)
           endif ()
 
+          if (USE_GSTREAMER_MPEGTS)
+              list(APPEND GSTREAMER_COMPONENTS mpegts)
+          endif ()
+
           if (ENABLE_WEB_AUDIO)
               list(APPEND GSTREAMER_COMPONENTS audio fft)
           endif ()
